            <ArticleTitle>The Airborne Visible / Infrared Imaging Spectrometer AVIS: Design, Characterization and Calibration.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1934-1953</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3390/s7091934</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Airborne Visible / Infrared imaging Spectrometer AVIS is a hyperspectralimager designed for environmental monitoring purposes. The sensor, which wasconstructed entirely from commercially available components, has been successfullydeployed during several experiments between 1999 and 2007. We describe the instrumentdesign and present the results of laboratory characterization and calibration of the system'ssecond generation, AVIS-2, which is currently being operated. The processing of the datais described and examples of remote sensing reflectance data are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
